     [ 0.   -0.88 -0.35]
     [ 0.    2.37 -0.88]]

    By contrast, the complex form is truly upper-triangular:

    >>> with jnp.printoptions(precision=2, suppress=True):
    ...   print(Tc)
    [[ 3.76+0.j    1.29-0.78j  2.02-0.5j ]
     [ 0.  +0.j   -0.88+0.91j -2.02+0.j  ]
     [ 0.  +0.j    0.  +0.j   -0.88-0.91j]]

